A||||6||Standard||Earl's braided steel hoses||||14||
Z||000000||Standard||04-26-2000||02:38 PM||||Just got the set in the mail today from the Fiero Store, only took 2 days!  They look great.  the only thing they didn't come with was some nuts and bolts to replace the rivits for the hose clamp.. but, at $95.95 for a set of 4, including shipping, they're cheaper than 4 rubber hoses w/o shipping!  they're so purty I don't want to hide them behind the wheel..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000001||fiero56||04-26-2000||02:55 PM||||Let me know how you like them after installing. I want to know if there is any change in pedal feel.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Standard||04-26-2000||02:58 PM||||There should be.. the hoses on my car right now are cracked, and the brakes need to be bled.. I'll let ya know!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Foh Fum||04-26-2000||03:49 PM||||Standard, <P>You're gonna love 'em!  I just came back from a test drive 2 hours ago after getting those on.  What a difference!  In addition to the braided steel brake lines though I also put The Fiero Stores 'big bore' master cylinder in as well.  Don't know which is most responsible but the combo is...Terrific!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Foh Fum (edited 04-26-2000).]||||reg||14
Z||000004||Foh Fum||04-26-2000||04:07 PM||||fiero56,<P>The pedal is firm and solid!  I mean, it's great!  <P>Someone on this forum suggested this combination to deal with spongy brakes on the Fiero.  I'd like to thank whoever it was but, researching my tracks, I couldn't find the post so I hope he sees it here.<P>Thanks!<P>Fum||||reg||14
Z||000005||mrfiero||04-27-2000||12:44 PM||||A couple of things.....first, I believe that the factory hoses are braided, but have a rubber outer covering.  I just did some work on my '88 GT and noticed a crack in one of the hoses.....I peeled it back and it was braided metal underneath.  <P>Another thing......you can buy a set of factory replacements for around $60 through carparts.com.  The fronts were $15.86 each and the rears were $12 and some change apiece.<P>I would imagine you would have felt the same difference in your brake feel whether you used the braided lines or the factory rubber ones.  Just the fact that they are new accounts for a lot of the improvement.<P>That said, I have used the braided steel lines on several of my Fieros and have nothing bad to say about them.  If anything they do look better than the rubber ones! ||||reg||1
Z||000006||batboy||04-27-2000||07:36 PM||||I think that was me that suggested new brake hoses. The braided hoses look much better and usually last longer. The regular hoses have a nylon reinforcement woven through the hose, I believe. Mr. Fiero's right, new hoses are new hoses. Old hoses suck.||||reg||1
